('CIT_ADMETE_CAT','ENT_ADMETE','SRC_HESIOD_THEOGONY','Hesiod, Theogony','Theogony 346-366','Peitho, and Admete, and Ianthe, and Electra, and Doris, and Prymno, and Urania divine in form, Hippo, Clymene, Rhodea, and Callirrhoe, Zeuxo and Clytie, and Idyia, and Pasithoe, Plexaura, and Galaxaura, and lovely Dione, Melobosis and Thoe and handsome Polydora, Cerceis lovely of form, and soft eyed Pluto, Perseis, Ianeira, Acaste, Xanthe, Petraea the fair, Menestho, and Europa, Metis, and Eurynome, and Telesto saffron-clad, Chryseis and Asia and charming Calypso, Eudora, and Tyche, Amphirho, and Ocyrrhoe, and Styx who is the chiefest of them all.','Hugh G. Evelyn-White',1914,'https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/348',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'Named in the catalogue; verify the line/stanza.',DATE '2026-06-26','name + substring gate against Evelyn-White Theogony (Gutenberg #348)',1),
